B.aX7=new A.bh(B.aXX,["Calculation: Outs Recorded \xf7 3\n\nInnings Pitched \u2014 total outs recorded divided by 3. Includes strikeouts, batted-ball outs, double plays, and pickoffs/throwouts.","Calculation: (Earned Runs \xd7 9) \xf7 Innings Pitched\n\nEarned Run Average \u2014 earned runs allowed per 9 innings. Lower is better; the classic measure of run prevention.","Calculation: (Walks + Hits) \xf7 Innings Pitched\n\nWalks + Hits per Inning Pitched. Measures how many baserunners you allow per inning. Lower is better.","Calculation: Hits Allowed \xf7 At-Bats\n\nOpponent Batting Average \u2014 how often batters get a hit against you. Lower is better.","Calculation: Total Bases Allowed \xf7 At-Bats\n\nOpponent Slugging % \u2014 measures the power (not just frequency) of contact allowed. Lower is better.","Calculation: Total Pitches \xf7 Plate Appearances\n\nPitches per Plate Appearance \u2014 a measure of efficiency; lower means you're working batters faster.","Calculation: (Strikeouts \xf7 Plate Appearances) \xd7 100\n\nStrikeout Percentage \u2014 how often you strike batters out. Higher is better.","Calculation: (Walks \xf7 Plate Appearances) \xd7 100\n\nWalk Percentage \u2014 how often you walk batters. Lower is better.","Calculation: K% \u2212 BB%\n\nStrikeout-minus-Walk Percentage \u2014 a single number combining strikeout and command ability; considered one of the best predictors of pitching success. Higher is better.","Calculation: (Swinging Misses \xf7 Total Swings) \xd7 100\n\nSwinging Strike Percentage \u2014 how often a swing results in a miss. Higher is better.","Calculation: First-Pitch Strikes \xf7 Total Plate Appearances \xd7 100\n\nFirst-Pitch Strike Percentage \u2014 pitches of a plate appearance that were strikes (called, swinging, foul, or in play), out of total plate appearances. Getting ahead in the count early. Higher is better."],t.l)
